come B**: build a new evaluation service serving direct launches and the\n    Llama Stack eval provider API\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The recommendation document compares both options against the full requirement\n  set with an explicit per-requirement verdict\n- A single outcome (A or B) is selected and recorded with rationale\n- The consumer-facing interface (CRD/API surface) is described at a level\n  sufficient for the Dashboard, pipeline-step, and Llama Stack provider work to\n  build against\n- The recommendation identifies where the execution code lives (existing repo or\n  new repo), and, if a new repo is required, the additional onboarding work is\n  called out\n- The recommendation is reviewed and accepted by the owning team\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (indirect — determines the execution path the launch capability builds on)\n- HLR-7 (indirect — determines how the Llama Stack eval provider API is backed)\n\nAddresses the strategy's open question 1 (execution engine).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47231,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be02543ae7df991c","agent_id":"aa255b350f855b6df","session_id":"a8243e44-1386-4db8-ba04-4dee4477cf9e","uuid":"582d5c25-1351-4b02-94f4-4d354af0ba7e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:39:38.616Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002 strategy"}
