{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-6230109b-d65c-4281-9e1b-8159eb9c16ef","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7a1df0d13dc6c27","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9002-m9n6px5h/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-A-E009.md","content":"# Evaluation execution and result persistence on the LMEvalJob path\n\n## Description\n\nConditional epic, planned under outcome A of the evaluation execution engine\ninvestigation: TrustyAI's LMEvalJob (which already wraps lm-evaluation-harness) is\nextended into the single execution path for platform evaluations. This epic\ndelivers the execution backend: launching evaluations of served models against\nselected benchmark suites, running custom evaluation tasks through the same flow,\npersisting results linked to the Model Registry version of the evaluated model, and\nrecording cost/duration metadata.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Extend the LMEvalJob-based execution so an evaluation can be launched against a\n  model served on the platform (KServe endpoint or Llama Stack distribution) with\n  a selected benchmark suite (standard out-of-the-box or user-defined custom task)\n- Expose the launch/status/results interface that the Dashboard, the Data Science\n  Pipelines evaluation step, and the Llama Stack eval provider build against\n- Persist evaluation results to Model Registry custom properties on the evaluated\n  model's version, in the canonical result schema, linking each run to the model\n  version it evaluated\n- Support user-defined custom evaluation tasks (own datasets and metrics) through\n  the same launch flow as standard suites\n- Record cost/duration metadata per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) for\n  capacity planning\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- An evaluation of a model served via a KServe endpoint or a Llama Stack\n  distribution can be launched against a selected suite and runs to completion\n  with per-benchmark scores\n- Results are persisted and linked to the Model Registry model version of the\n  evaluated model, in the canonical result schema, and remain interpretable across\n  benchmark-suite version bumps\n- A user-defined custom evaluation task (own dataset and metrics) can be run\n  through the same flow as a standard suite\n- Each run records cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time)\n- The launch/status/results interface is available for the Dashboard, pipeline\n  step, and Llama Stack provider consumers\n- Selected out-of-the-box suites are available to the execution path (bundled or\n  customer-fetched per the licensing determination)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (execution backend for launching evaluations of served models)\n- HLR-3 (results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version)\n- HLR-4 (custom evaluation tasks through the same flow)\n- HLR-8 (cost/duration metadata recording)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":57659,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be02543ae7df991c","agent_id":"aa255b350f855b6df","session_id":"a8243e44-1386-4db8-ba04-4dee4477cf9e","uuid":"0bc17b88-50f9-43c5-b0d1-59b9a715ca30","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:41:16.202Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9002 strategy"}
