{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fbcbfddd65342eb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-BRANCH-B-E009\n3\ttitle: Evaluation execution and result persistence via a new evaluation service\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation recommends building on LMEvalJob (outcome\n17\t    A), this epic is removed and execution is planned under the LMEvalJob-path branch\n18\t    instead; any new-repo onboarding work in this branch is then unnecessary.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Evaluation execution and result persistence via a new evaluation service\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional epic, planned under outcome B of the evaluation execution engine\n40\tinvestigation: a new evaluation service is built as the platform's execution path,\n41\tserving both direct evaluation launches and the Llama Stack eval provider API.\n42\tThis epic delivers the execution backend: the service, its launch/status/results\n43\tinterface, running standard and custom benchmark suites against served models,\n44\tpersisting results linked to the Model Registry version of the evaluated model,\n45\tand recording cost/duration metadata.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Build the evaluation service in the TrustyAI component's midstream repository\n50\t  (per the investigation's recommendation; if a new repository is recommended\n51\t  instead, this branch is extended with repo/license/Konflux onboarding work\n52\t  before this epic can start)\n53\t- Use lm-evaluation-harness as the benchmark execution engine, consistent with the\n54\t  platform's existing lm-eval task naming\n55\t- Launch evaluations against models served on the platform (KServe endpoints or\n56\t  Llama Stack distributions) with a selected benchmark suite (standard\n57\t  out-of-the-box or user-defined custom task)\n58\t- Expose the launch/status/results interface that the Dashboard, the Data Science\n59\t  Pipelines evaluation step, and the Llama Stack eval provider build against,\n60\t  including the service-side backing for the Llama Stack eval provider API\n61\t- Persist evaluation results to Model Registry custom properties on the evaluated\n62\t  model's version, in the canonical result schema, linking each run to the model\n63\t  version it evaluated\n64\t- Record cost/duration metadata per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) for\n65\t  capacity planning\n66\t\n67\t## Acceptance Criteria\n68\t\n69\t- An evaluation of a model served via a KServe endpoint or a Llama Stack\n70\t  distribution can be launched against a selected suite and runs to completion\n71\t  with per-benchmark scores\n72\t- The service backs the Llama Stack eval provider API surface with the same\n73\t  results as direct launches\n74\t- Results are persisted and linked to the Model Registry model version of the\n75\t  evaluated model, in the canonical result schema, and remain interpretable across\n76\t  benchmark-suite version bumps\n77\t- A user-defined custom evaluation task (own dataset and metrics) can be run\n78\t  through the same flow as a standard suite\n79\t- Each run records cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time)\n80\t- The launch/status/results interface is available for the Dashboard, pipeline\n81\t  step, and Llama Stack provider consumers\n82\t- Selected out-of-the-box suites are available to the execution path (bundled or\n83\t  customer-fetched per the licensing determination)\n84\t- If the service lands in a new repository, its build pipeline is green before\n85\t  this epic completes\n86\t\n87\t## HLR Traceability\n88\t\n89\t- HLR-1 (execution backend for launching evaluations of served models)\n90\t- HLR-3 (results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version)\n91\t- HLR-4 (custom evaluation tasks through the same flow)\n92\t- HLR-7 (service-side backing for the Llama Stack eval provider API)\n93\t- HLR-8 (cost/duration metadata recording)\n94\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83314622072566be","agent_id":"aaf5de986d62553a8","session_id":"a8243e44-1386-4db8-ba04-4dee4477cf9e","uuid":"72ed9a03-0aff-453a-b0d2-3775c79ce246","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:55:00.595Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fbcbfddd65342eb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
