{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-962ff79d582667fc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: evaluation execution engine — extend LMEvalJob or build a new\n4\t  evaluation service'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n6\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n7\tteam: TrustyAI\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n16\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: evaluation execution engine — extend LMEvalJob or build a new evaluation service\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolves the strategy's first open question: whether the platform evaluation\n31\tcapability builds on TrustyAI's LMEvalJob (Tech Preview, already wrapping\n32\tlm-evaluation-harness) as the single execution path, or whether a new evaluation\n33\tservice is needed that can also serve Llama Stack's eval provider API. The\n34\tdeliverable is a written recommendation, with an architecture sketch of the chosen\n35\texecution path and the consumer-facing interface (CR/API) that the Dashboard, the\n36\tData Science Pipelines step, and the Llama Stack eval provider will build against.\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Assess LMEvalJob's current capabilities and Tech Preview limitations against the\n41\t  full requirement set: standard and custom benchmark tasks, result persistence to\n42\t  Model Registry, cost/duration metadata recording, and backing the Llama Stack\n43\t  eval provider API\n44\t- Assess what a new evaluation service would require, including where it would live\n45\t  (the TrustyAI component's midstream repo vs a new repository — if a new\n46\t  repository is recommended, repo/license/Konflux onboarding epics must be added to\n47\t  that branch of the plan)\n48\t- Define the consumer-facing interface for launching evaluations and reading run\n49\t  status and results, sufficient for downstream consumers to build against\n50\t- Confirm the chosen path serves both direct evaluation launches and the Llama\n51\t  Stack eval provider API\n52\t- Record the decision as one of two bounded outcomes:\n53\t  - **Outcome A**: extend LMEvalJob as the single execution path\n54\t  - **Outcome B**: build a new evaluation service serving direct launches and the\n55\t    Llama Stack eval provider API\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- The recommendation document compares both options against the full requirement\n60\t  set with an explicit per-requirement verdict\n61\t- A single outcome (A or B) is selected and recorded with rationale\n62\t- The consumer-facing interface (CRD/API surface) is described at a level\n63\t  sufficient for the Dashboard, pipeline-step, and Llama Stack provider work to\n64\t  build against\n65\t- The recommendation identifies where the execution code lives (existing repo or\n66\t  new repo), and, if a new repo is required, the additional onboarding work is\n67\t  called out\n68\t- The recommendation is reviewed and accepted by the owning team\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-1 (indirect — determines the execution path the launch capability builds on)\n73\t- HLR-7 (indirect — determines how the Llama Stack eval provider API is backed)\n74\t\n75\tAddresses the strategy's open question 1 (execution engine).\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab900bb5d18f93ef","agent_id":"a404d519e095e1902","session_id":"a8243e44-1386-4db8-ba04-4dee4477cf9e","uuid":"581f0aba-0244-444c-89f6-6190d80f6c67","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:57:45.440Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-962ff79d582667fc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
