{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3e31f759089b15d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: canonical evaluation result schema for Model Registry persistence'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: Model Registry\n6\tteam: Model Registry\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: High\n19\tai_implementability_score: 3\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: canonical evaluation result schema for Model Registry persistence\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's second open question: the canonical format for evaluation\n30\tresults persisted to Model Registry custom properties on the evaluated model's\n31\tversion. The schema is prototyped against real MMLU output before being committed,\n32\tand must survive benchmark-suite version bumps. Owned by the Model Registry team\n33\tbecause the persistence target (custom properties on ModelVersion entities) is\n34\ttheir extension point; the outcome is the data contract for the execution,\n35\tDashboard, and Llama Stack provider work.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Run representative standard benchmark (MMLU) evaluations and capture the raw\n40\t  lm-evaluation-harness output\n41\t- Design the canonical result structure: per-benchmark scores, suite identity and\n42\t  version, run metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time), and the link to the\n43\t  evaluated model version\n44\t- Validate the structure against Model Registry custom properties (REST API,\n45\t  type/size constraints, queryability for comparison views)\n46\t- Confirm the structure remains interpretable when a benchmark suite is upgraded\n47\t  (versioned suite identity recorded with results)\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- A prototype persists real MMLU evaluation results to a Model Registry model\n52\t  version's custom properties and reads them back correctly\n53\t- The schema records suite name and version so persisted results remain\n54\t  interpretable after a benchmark-suite version bump\n55\t- The schema carries the cost/duration metadata fields (tokens, wall-clock, GPU\n56\t  time) required for capacity planning\n57\t- The schema recommendation is documented and agreed with the Model Registry team,\n58\t  and shared with the teams building the execution path, the pipelines evaluation\n59\t  step, Dashboard views, and Llama Stack provider\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- HLR-3 (defines the persisted, version-linked result format)\n64\t- HLR-8 (defines the cost/duration metadata fields recorded per run)\n65\t- Enables HLR-5 (Dashboard reads the schema), HLR-6 (the pipelines evaluation\n66\t  step exposes scores in the schema), and HLR-7 (provider returns results\n67\t  in the schema)\n68\t\n69\tAddresses the strategy's open question 2 (result schema).\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab900bb5d18f93ef","agent_id":"a404d519e095e1902","session_id":"a8243e44-1386-4db8-ba04-4dee4477cf9e","uuid":"0636b3c0-f108-4dda-bc75-e0ad50875bc4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:57:46.294Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3e31f759089b15d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
