{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a596016092d82c06","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9002-E003\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: benchmark dataset licensing for disconnected redistribution'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9002\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Investigation: benchmark dataset licensing for disconnected redistribution\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tResolves the strategy's third open question: which standard benchmark suites can be\n30\tredistributed with the platform in disconnected environments, and which must be\n31\tfetched by the customer. The deliverable is a per-suite classification with cited\n32\tlicense terms and legal confirmation, which determines the scope of the\n33\tout-of-the-box benchmark suite catalog.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- License review of the candidate standard suites (e.g. MMLU, ARC, HellaSwag and\n38\t  other lm-eval task families under consideration) and the datasets they load\n39\t- Classify each suite: redistributable in the product vs customer-fetched, with the\n40\t  governing license terms cited per suite\n41\t- Identify the fallback delivery mechanism for suites that cannot be redistributed\n42\t  (customer-supplied datasets in disconnected environments)\n43\t- Obtain legal confirmation of the redistribution determinations\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Every candidate suite is classified as redistributable or customer-fetched, with\n48\t  the specific license terms cited\n49\t- Redistribution determinations are confirmed through legal review\n50\t- The final list of out-of-the-box (bundled) suites vs customer-fetched suites is\n51\t  produced and handed to the benchmark suite availability work as its input\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- HLR-2 (determines which standard suites can ship out of the box)\n56\t\n57\tAddresses the strategy's open question 3 (benchmark dataset licensing).\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab900bb5d18f93ef","agent_id":"a404d519e095e1902","session_id":"a8243e44-1386-4db8-ba04-4dee4477cf9e","uuid":"83e01152-e0e0-485a-9c66-3aa9ceaeb7f9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:57:47.192Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a596016092d82c06","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
