\tit risks exceeding the ~2-week epic size: if outcome B is selected, this branch\n49\tis decomposed further at resolution time (e.g. service core, persistence, and\n50\tprovider backing as separate epics continuing the ID sequence) before\n51\timplementation is scheduled.\n52\t\n53\t## Scope\n54\t\n55\t- Build the evaluation service in the TrustyAI component's midstream repository\n56\t  (per the investigation's recommendation; if a new repository is recommended\n57\t  instead, this branch is extended with repo/license/Konflux onboarding work\n58\t  before this epic can start)\n59\t- Use lm-evaluation-harness as the benchmark execution engine, consistent with the\n60\t  platform's existing lm-eval task naming\n61\t- Launch evaluations against models served on the platform (KServe endpoints or\n62\t  Llama Stack distributions) with a selected benchmark suite (standard\n63\t  out-of-the-box or user-defined custom task)\n64\t- Expose the launch/status/results interface that the Dashboard, the Data Science\n65\t  Pipelines evaluation step, and the Llama Stack eval provider build against,\n66\t  including the service-side backing for the Llama Stack eval provider API\n67\t- Persist evaluation results to Model Registry custom properties on the evaluated\n68\t  model's version, in the canonical result schema, linking each run to the model\n69\t  version it evaluated\n70\t- Record cost/duration metadata per run (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time) for\n71\t  capacity planning\n72\t\n73\t## Acceptance Criteria\n74\t\n75\t- An evaluation of a model served via a KServe endpoint or a Llama Stack\n76\t  distribution can be launched against a selected suite and runs to completion\n77\t  with per-benchmark scores\n78\t- The service backs the Llama Stack eval provider API surface with the same\n79\t  results as direct launches\n80\t- Results are persisted and linked to the Model Registry model version of the\n81\t  evaluated model, in the canonical result schema, and remain interpretable across\n82\t  benchmark-suite version bumps\n83\t- A user-defined custom evaluation task (own dataset and metrics) can be run\n84\t  through the same flow as a standard suite\n85\t- Each run records cost/duration metadata (tokens, wall-clock, GPU time)\n86\t- The launch/status/results interface is available for the Dashboard, pipeline\n87\t  step, and Llama Stack provider consumers\n88\t- Selected out-of-the-box suites are available to the execution path (bundled or\n89\t  customer-fetched per the licensing determination)\n90\t- If the service lands in a new repository, its build pipeline is green before\n91\t  this epic completes\n92\t\n93\t## HLR Traceability\n94\t\n95\t- HLR-1 (execution backend for launching evaluations of served models)\n96\t- HLR-3 (results persisted and linked to the Model Registry version)\n97\t- HLR-4 (custom evaluation tasks through the same flow)\n98\t- HLR-7 (service-side backing for the Llama Stack eval provider API)\n99\t- HLR-8 (cost/duration metadata recording)\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab900bb5d18f93ef","agent_id":"a404d519e095e1902","session_id":"a8243e44-1386-4db8-ba04-4dee4477cf9e","uuid":"ebba2ddc-c4d8-472c-b2ec-aea0e5e0bd3d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:58:00.067Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b33f3e9f33257674","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9002 decomposition"}
